  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="cb78865a-668e-50ec-872a-e6d402531dc6" activityNameId="bc1b1466-57f8-5024-911b-3da3ac705379" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Single-Si wafer, electronics, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Single-Si wafer, electronics, at plant
The reference flow for the life cycle inventory is 1 square metre of wafer surface. The sc-Silicon columns are sawn into square wafers with a size 156x156 mm2 (0.0243 m2) and a thickness of 190 um. The weight is 443 g/m2. The sawing losses are 443g/m2.;
Synonyms: monocrystalline, single crystalline, silicon; 
UUID: cca7606e-a8a5-312c-b576-3ea0ced65b95
Sawing and cleaning of wafers. The process data include electricity use, water and working material consumption (e.g. stainless steel for saw-blades, argon gas, hydrofluoric and hydrochloric acid). Production wastes to be treated and process-specific NOx- and waterborne pollutants are considered. No data on other process specific air emissions.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Use of multi wire saws.
Time period: Collection of data in 2005. Use of data from an environmental report of a production plant (ca. 3 million wafers per year) and some data from older publications.
Production volume: 3.6E4 m2 in 2005
Sampling: Data collection by factory representatives. Environmental report and LCA studies. 
Extrapolations: own estimation with data for PV wafer
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cca7606e-a8a5-312c-b576-3ea0ced65b95.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
